  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 57\u2011year\u2011old male with a lifelong history of diabetes\u2011related kidney disease that has progressed from CKD stage 1 in the early 1950s to CKD stage 4 by the late 1970s. Hypertension has been present since 1950 and is treated with lisinopril and hydrochlorothiazide, but recent blood pressure values are unavailable. He has obesity, metabolic syndrome, and anemia, all contributing to cardiovascular and renal risk. Osteoarthritis of the hip causes chronic pain managed with naproxen, a nephrotoxic NSAID in the setting of advanced CKD. Social factors include part\u2011time employment, a criminal record, intimate\u2011partner abuse, limited social contact and social isolation, which may affect adherence and access to care. He is awaiting kidney transplantation. Insulin therapy is documented despite a reported pre\u2011diabetes diagnosis and a low A1c, suggesting possible undocumented diabetes.",
